       From now on, running it without  arguments  is  equivalent  to  ooppeennssssll
       hheellpp.

       The error return values from some control calls (ctrl) have changed

       One  significant  change  is  that controls which used to return -2 for
       invalid inputs, now return -1  indicating  a  generic  error  condition
       instead.

       DH and DHX key types have different settable parameters

       Previously  (in  1.1.1)  these conflicting parameters were allowed, but
       will now result in errors. See EEVVPP__PPKKEEYY--DDHH(7) for further details. This
       affects  the  behaviour  of   ooppeennssssll--ggeennppkkeeyy(1)   for   DH   parameter
       generation.

